\DOC extend_rectype_net

\TYPE {extend_rectype_net : string * ('a * 'b * thm) -> unit}

\SYNOPSIS
Extends internal store of distinctness and injectivity theorems for a new
inductive type.

\DESCRIBE
HOL Light maintains several data structures based on the current set of
distinctness and injectivity theorems for the inductive data type so far
defined. A call {extend_rectype_net ("tyname",(_,_,rth))} where {rth} is the
recursion theorem for the type as returned as the second item from
{define_type}, extends these structures for a new type: the injectivity theorem
proved by {prove_constructors_injective} is added to {injectivity_store} and as
rewrites to {basic_rectype_net}; the conversions produced by
{constructors_distinct_convs} are added to {basic_rectype_net} and
{constructors_distinct_net}; and a function that proves the distinctness
theorem the first time it is called is added to {distinctness_store}. Two
arguments are ignored just for regularity with some other internal data
structures.

\FAILURE
Never fails, even if the theorem is malformed.

\COMMENTS
This function is called automatically by {define_type}, and normally users will
not need to invoke it explicitly. For a mutually recursive family of types,
{define_type} calls it only for the first type, since the recursion theorem
covers them all, and enters the same theorems for the other types in
{distinctness_store} and {injectivity_store}.

\SEEALSO
basic_rectype_net, constructors_distinct_convs, constructors_distinct_net,
define_type, distinctness_store, injectivity_store.
\ENDDOC
